  "Question": "Three semicircles of radius \\(1\\) are constructed on diameter \\(\\overline{AB}\\) of a semicircle of radius \\(2.\\) The centers of the small semicircles divide \\(\\overline{AB}\\) into four line segments of equal length, as shown. What is the area of the shaded region that lies within the large semicircle but outside the smaller semicircles?\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2003_AMC_12B_Q16_question_fig1.svg)",
